                <pb facs="1128" n="1118" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1118"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.801/7–749: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Douglas</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-07T18:00:00+01:00">July 7, 1949—6 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 7—5:39 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2649. Canton’s Cantel 670 and 673 to Department re closure Chinese ports.
                    Scarlett, Foreign Office, states Foreign Office considering reply to latest
                    Chinese note but will require ministerial conference for approval. Also that in
                    his personal opinion it very doubtful that British Government would consent
                    convoy British merchant ships through waters closed by Nationalists.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Douglas</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
